{# newsLedger(items, caption) — news as a dated ledger: one mono date column,
   one item column, hairline between rows.

   No header row and no kind column. With two columns, a header row labels what
   the rows already make obvious, and it put a second ink bar directly beneath
   the section band. The `kind` field is still carried in each item's front
   matter but is not rendered: the item text already says whether it is a paper,
   an award, or a talk. The visually-hidden caption keeps the table announced.

   Dates show month and year only: the day a paper was accepted is not
   something a reader uses. The <time datetime> attribute still carries the
   full calendar date for machines. #}
{% macro newsLedger(items, caption) %}
  <table class="data-table ledger">
    <caption class="visually-hidden">{{ caption }}</caption>
    <tbody>
      {% for item in items %}
        <tr>
          <td class="ledger-date"><time datetime="{{ item.date | isoDate }}">{{ item.date | monthYear }}</time></td>
          <td class="ledger-item">{{ item.content | safe }}</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
{% endmacro %}
